-- issue #1040: a `where`-GROUP helper (`d`) is called at TWO DIFFERENT ground
-- types (`Int` and `Bool`) from within the SAME top-level binding's body.
-- `medaka check` exits 0 (`top : String` inferred, `d`'s constraint generalized
-- over both call sites). `medaka run` (the interpreter) correctly REJECTS at
-- runtime with an E-PANIC (`intToString: not an Int`) because it dispatches
-- `debug` using a type pinned from ONE of the two call sites. The NATIVE build
-- is worse: it builds and runs with exit 0, printing `11` -- both calls silently
-- resolve to the SAME (wrong) monomorphized `d`, so `d True` prints `1` instead
-- of `True`. This is the SILENT cell: a wrong answer with no diagnostic and no
-- crash anywhere in the pipeline.
top : String
top = d (1 : Int) ++ d True
  where
    d v = debug v

main = println top
